id: pm-slack-standup-progress-evidence
title: Report progress gains with evidence revisions across standup windows
description: "Deliver a read-only typed SDK and compact CLI projection of passing test facts, explicitly accepted criterion evidence and declared readiness changes. Reuse SDK verified history and canonical item reads; preserve lifecycle activity as separate counts."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-slack-standup#164"
created_at: "2026-10-28T23:07:24.361Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T18:36:51.668Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-29T18:36:50.355Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-29T18:36:50.355Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: A status-only edit never appears as verified progress; Each reported gain names its evidence revision; The same evidence is not counted twice across reporting windows
release: 2026.10.29
comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T23:07:32.517Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: standup lifecycle sections and compare snapshots count statuses; core PmClient.listAllComplete, history verification/replay and native linked tests supply facts; pm-review reviewCoverage supplies reviewed/gap attention, explicitly not acceptance. pm-evidence supplies source freshness. None delivers periodic evidence gains deduplicated against verified item history. Implement a read-only projection with caller-held revision checkpoints, native passing tests, and strict explicit accepted/readiness declarations; never infer acceptance from reviewed or status. No tracker writes, imports, sync, journaled apply, shared checkpoints or background delivery are added."
  "2026-10-28T23:21:16.762Z",codex-agent,"Focused evidence and no-git CLI checks pass: status/comment-only windows have zero gains; original revision citations, deterministic retries, deduplicated older runs and normalized declaration replays are covered. Public validation at source head 5c10bafbca1b9d0399a562cf8d4ac503ab345d99: read-only non-git copy, git absent from PATH, 106 items, 1008 history events, 106 pages, 258 status activity events, 222 comment activity events, 235 foreign annotations, zero gains/refusals/replay gains; all 218 source files byte-unchanged. Zero recorded passing runs or explicit acceptance/readiness declarations is reported honestly, with no inference from green prose. Full npm/Bun gates will run in CI at unchanged coverage and duplication thresholds."
  "2026-10-28T23:27:24.900Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof in disposable copies: removing deduplication, omitting targetRevision from evidence identity, or citing the final window revision for every gain each failed the native-results regression (3/3 failed as required). The restored implementation passed the same selected regression 1/1. The first 500-sequence real-SDK model passed 1500 native state mutations with zero mismatches, including relationship/body preservation and whitespace/CRLF old-input replays. A final model pass adds random ambient focus and bounded fixture cleanup. Focused module checks passed 7/7 and measured 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines; per-read-boundary peer appends are observed once across returned prefixes. No journaled apply or shared checkpoint mutation exists in this read-only feature."
  "2026-10-28T23:33:23.546Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted checks: native linked runner 1/1 commands and 7/7 tests passed, with automatic recording correctly left disabled by existing project policy. Current focused CLI/module/smoke checks passed 13/13; the module measured 100 percent in all four coverage dimensions. Public validation was repeated after switching checkpoint and evidence hashes to the SDK canonical history primitives, with identical 106-item/1008-event measurements, zero refusals and all 218 files unchanged. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstrings and changelog generation/check passed. Full npm/Bun acceptance and packed npm/Bun global/local hosts remain the CI release-gate responsibility."
  "2026-10-28T23:35:10.444Z",codex-agent,"Final seeded model with random ambient focus passed 500/500 operation sequences and 1500 native state mutations, with zero SDK read-back mismatches. Per-sequence SDK cleanup keeps the shared non-git fixture bounded. All requested code, SDK/CLI, strict input/output validation, docs, public-data probe and interleaving/revert evidence are complete. No pm CLI/SDK defect was found; linked-result persistence remains intentionally disabled by existing policy. Release this claim for orchestrator verification; leave the item in progress. CI release gates at the final pushed head, including all six packed host scenarios, are the remaining external check and will be linked on the PR."
  "2026-10-28T23:42:35.227Z",codex-agent,"Final contract review tightened the seeded model to choose random clear-both, clear-comments, clear-runs or status-only operations before replay, with intermediate SDK read-back. Checkpoints now hash canonical SDK item identity so their bounded token length does not depend on legacy id length; operator ids defer to SDK normalization instead of applying the evidence display-label limit. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/pull/164 remains ready for review; final-head CI will supersede the first queued run."
  "2026-10-28T23:48:32.363Z",codex-agent,"The strengthened random-operation model exposed a test-oracle projection distinction: SDK full reads represent some empty collections explicitly, while the native canonical write format omits them. Both reference and SDK-read-back states now pass through canonicalDocument before comparison, without hand-written normalization. The focused final feature tests pass 7/7 at 100 percent module coverage in all four dimensions; canonical SDK primitives also loaded successfully from the packed minimum host 2026.10.20. The strengthened 500-sequence model is running and CI will validate the final head. Automated review receipts contain skips, budget/trial limits or neutral results and are not approval."
  "2026-10-28T23:53:38.799Z",codex-agent,"CI at the earlier head reached 296 tests per Linux lane: 295 pass and one source-copy guide test fails because its hard-coded root module list omits progress-deltas.ts; all 14 authored sources measured 100 percent in all four dimensions, and Windows passed six packed host scenarios. The guide fixture now copies all root TypeScript modules so future source additions remain valid. This is a fixture correction, not a lowered gate. The final strengthened model has reached 400 sequences without mismatches; final-head CI will be restarted after the focused guide probe passes."
  "2026-10-28T23:54:44.030Z",codex-agent,"The final strengthened model passed 500/500 random operation sequences and 1500 native mutations with zero mismatches, including intermediate SDK-normalized read-back, status-only/partial removal operations, replay, relationships, body preservation and random ambient focus. The independent final source public probe again returned 106 items and 1008 verified events with zero gains/refusals/replay gains and 218/218 unchanged files. The source-copy fixture correction is the only remaining code adjustment before the final CI push."
  "2026-10-28T23:55:55.940Z",codex-agent,The corrected source-only guide probe passed 1/1 and executed its documented typecheck/build/lint/docstring/duplication and decision/export/unit commands without dist. Final CI must rerun npm and Bun release gates at the new pushed head; previous-head failures remain recorded rather than being treated as approval. Final local feature/model/public evidence is complete.
  "2026-10-29T00:08:30.158Z",codex-agent,"CI wait cutoff reached for source head ac4e55841faba389f71225eea37e26fed7031bf4. Run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/actions/runs/40790743598: Node 26 passed npm run release:check AND bun run release:check, each 296/296 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 14 authored sources at 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines, canonical reader 1/1 and packed hosts 6/6. Windows passed 22 launcher tests with 13 platform skips, zero failures, plus packed hosts 6/6. Node 22.18.0 remains in progress in the full npm/Bun release step at the cutoff. Reviews with skipped, neutral, quota or trial outcomes are missing review evidence. This append-only tracker receipt changes no runtime code; its pushed head also requires fresh CI and is not claimed certified. Stop waiting under the queue limit; the orchestrator pipeline can continue verification."
  "2026-10-29T00:20:00.764Z",codex-agent,"Re-review scope: both blockers violate the read-only boundary and stable typed-refusal contract. Package-wide search found two maintenance-capable history-command calls: progress deltas and the shared ordinary standup reader (also used by decisions, exports and aliases). Both will share SDK read-only snapshot/verification primitives, with no missing-stream maintenance or write hooks. Malformed or unavailable history will map to history_unavailable with exit 2 and remedy. Git status is clean and origin/main is already an ancestor, so no merge is required. Published review records contain no additional actionable non-blocking findings beyond the two supplied blockers."
  "2026-10-29T00:51:21.667Z",codex-agent,"Class-wide fix implemented: both SDK history-command calls are gone. Shared SDK locateItem/readHistorySnapshot/readLocatedItem/verifyHistoryEntries reads existing source only, preserving retained deleted streams and refusing progress over compacted history. SDK history/I/O/parse/current-document failures become native SDK-recognized ProgressRefusal history_unavailable, exit 2, with remedy and CLI required guidance. Adversarial suite passed 3/3: six malformed/missing/hash/conflict cases under strict_error and auto_create across direct SDK readers, all discovered commands and exports, plus JSON/default CLI paths with an installed onWrite probe. Authoritative bytes and mtimes are unchanged; progress also preserves derived files. Existing certified list calls can rebuild native runtime caches, which are not authoritative data. Actual native history maintenance is a positive control and triggers the installed write hook; report calls never do. Disposable behavioral reverts restoring native history maintenance or leaking history_json_invalid each failed the adversarial regression; restored shared reader passed. Packed npm/Bun local/global/npx/bunx acceptance now repeats missing/JSONL refusals under auto_create."
  "2026-10-29T01:11:25.115Z",codex-agent,"Full clean-identity npm release gate ran at two workers: 297/299 tests passed; both failures are the existing packed matrix child limit (290 seconds, ETIMEDOUT). The complete runtime source set, including progress-refusals and verified-history, measured 100 percent in all four dimensions; operational accept-packed coverage is incomplete because those subprocesses timed out, so the full gate is not claimed passed. All three adversarial tests and the 500-sequence model passed in that full run. No timeout or quality threshold was increased. Added public scenario-stage diagnostics to identify a stalled matrix phase; the serial full Bun gate follows."
  "2026-10-29T01:31:37.969Z",codex-agent,"Re-review validation complete locally: native linked runner executed the new regression, 1/1 command and 3/3 tests passed; result persistence remains disabled by existing project policy. Full npm and Bun release gates ran serially at two workers; each completed 297/299 tests, two packed matrix child timeouts at the unchanged 290-second limit, zero skips/cancellations. Both measured all runtime modules at 100 percent in all four coverage dimensions; operational matrix coverage is incomplete, so neither full local gate is claimed passed. Stage diagnostics reached npm-current and bun-current before timeout. Typecheck, test typecheck, build, lint, 16-source docstrings and zero duplication passed. Public read-only validation repeated: 106 items, 1008 events, zero refusals or replay gains, 218/218 unchanged files. Minimum SDK 2026.10.20 exposes all required supported primitives and native error class. No dependency bump or SDK gap. Current main is still an ancestor; no merge needed. Push the class-wide fix for fresh exact-head npm/Bun CI; leave the item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-29T02:58:15.224Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 violates qualification-before-deduplication and immutable first-evidence provenance: raw previous run-ID presence suppresses a later valid passing result. Package-wide search finds one native-run admission loop shared by SDK and CLI; declarations use full-record inspection and ordinary standup/decision/export paths do not project test gains. Replace raw-ID adjacency with the set of qualified passing identities at the preceding revision, while retaining the global evidence ledger for all older windows. Add failed/malformed correction, regression, removal and older-input replay coverage, including exact native historical read-back and packed consumers. Origin/main is already an ancestor and the worktree was clean, so no merge is needed. No other actionable published inline findings were present."
  "2026-10-29T03:07:23.368Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 focused proof: new correction suite passed 2/2, including the native linked runner (1/1 command, 2/2 tests; existing result tracking remains disabled). Eight unqualified native states preserve valid neighbors, qualify corrected IDs at the immediate native revision, retain original target/history provenance after removal and replay, and agree across page sizes 1/2/3, standalone/injected SDK readers, JSON and compact TOON CLI without git. SDK canonicalization owns fixture read-back; native compact-output omissions are preserved. Disposable behavioral revert of only the previous-ID eligibility check failed correction 0 immediately; restored qualified-identity code passed 1/1. No original tests were weakened. The model now includes random unqualified prefixes across 500 sequences and 2000 mutations, retaining existing relationship/body/ambient-focus/replay assertions. Packed acceptance adds failed and malformed corrections plus first-passing provenance checks to every installed consumer. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, 16-source docstrings and zero duplication passed."
  "2026-10-29T03:17:26.401Z",codex-agent,"Standalone npm run accept:packed passed all 6/6 installed scenarios with the round-2 correction/replay assertions: npm/Bun current 2026.10.25, npm/Bun minimum 2026.10.20, npm global and Bun global. The packed readers accepted native SDK fixture history without any version-floor or dependency change. Every scenario retains the round-1 malformed/missing-history, output-mode, immutability and status-only checks. Full npm and Bun release gates follow serially with at most two workers and unchanged limits."
  "2026-10-29T03:45:55.200Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 full local validation finished serially at two workers: npm run release:check AND bun run release:check each completed 299/301 tests, zero skips/cancellations, with only the two existing packed-matrix child timeouts at the unchanged 290-second limit. Both passed the correction regressions, round-1 read-only regressions and strengthened 500-sequence/2000-mutation SDK model with zero mismatches. Runtime modules measured 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines; whole-package operational coverage is incomplete because the matrix children timed out, so neither local full gate is claimed passed. Standalone npm run accept:packed passed all 6/6 current/minimum/global npm/Bun consumers, including both correction classes, output formats and stable first-passing provenance. Existing packed timing follow-up already covers shared-host timeouts; no duplicate item was created. Fresh exact-head CI remains required after push. No additional actionable non-blocking findings or SDK gaps were found."
  "2026-10-29T03:46:52.413Z",codex-agent,"Final round-2 public-data probe passed on the same read-only non-git public tracker at 5c10bafbca1b9d0399a562cf8d4ac503ab345d99: 106 items and pages, 1008 verified events, 258 status activities, 222 comment activities, 235 foreign annotations, zero passing/criterion/readiness gains, invalid records, refusals or replay gains; 218/218 source files unchanged and git unavailable. The code and tracker evidence are ready for the final source commit and exact-head CI. Release the own claim for orchestrator re-review, leaving the item in progress."
